      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T20:09:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "* **Unsafe Array Size Parameter in `ff_util.c` (`ft_get_time_local`):** `snprintf(time_buff, sizeof(buff), ...)` is unsafe. `sizeof(buff)` refers to the internal `char buff[64]`, but it is being used to dictate the bounds of the externally passed `time_buff` pointer. While `time_buff` happens to be `64` bytes in the current caller (`log_printf`), this is a latent buffer overflow risk.  \n    \n* *Suggestion:* Change the signature to `static void ft_get_time_local(char *time_buff, size_t time_buff_size)` and use `time_buff_size` in the `snprintf` call.",
