      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Memory Leak (Unfreed Device List)**\n\nThe author replied: \u0027No, after the device is found, it still goes to the error label and releases the resources.\u0027\n\nThis is mathematically impossible as written. When the device is found, `ret` is assigned `FT_SUCCESS` (which is `0`). Therefore, when execution hits `if (ret) {` on line 223, the condition evaluates to **false**, and it **skips** the `libusb_free_device_list` block entirely!\n\nFurthermore, `mbedtls_usb_connect()` calls `libusb_get_device_list(..., \u0026usb_ctx-\u003edevs);` *again*, which overwrites the `usb_ctx-\u003edevs` pointer. This permanently leaks the list that was allocated in this function. \n\n**Remediation:** You must unconditionally free the device list on the success path.",
